{"archetypes":[{"name":"timing-ledger","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff adds round timing records, report rendering, and deferred timing emitters across design and implement workflows.","prompt_body":"Investigate the new timing-ledger row format, duration arithmetic, parent/child ordering, idempotence, and report rendering paths. Pay special attention to stale environment variables, deferred round-start files, accepted/rejected count fallbacks, and compatibility with existing mark/vendor-task rows. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"workflow-resume","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff changes /design routing, pause/resume, SIMPLE/HARD classification, and persisted session state boundaries.","prompt_body":"Review the design route, pause-save, publish, and run-params changes as one workflow rather than isolated scripts. Check whether SIMPLE versus HARD classification, legacy sentinels, cancel routes, result-env emission, and session rehydration remain consistent across fresh, resumed, and paused runs. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"bash-parity","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The Python finalize/ship/CI changes are intended to mirror existing bash behavior while bash remains the shipped default.","prompt_body":"Compare the changed Python finalize, ship, run-log, merge, rebase, and CI-monitor paths against the intended bash-parity behavior in the plan. Focus on status-token mapping, preflight ordering, fail-closed recovery gates, local cleanup semantics, remote branch checks, and force-push behavior. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"runlog-recovery","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff touches manifest recovery, postmerge finalization, teardown log commits, and sentinel gating that affect committed run logs.","prompt_body":"Examine whether manifest recovery, partial/done transitions, final-report rendering, execution-issues flushing, and larch-log commits happen in the intended order. Check warning-only versus terminal failure behavior, PR-closed gating, post-merge sentinel creation, and default-branch refusal paths. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"ci-rebase","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The CI fix path now threads pending rebase state through monitor, state serialization, and push retries.","prompt_body":"Review the CI-fix stage-and-push flow for correct plain-push versus force-push selection after rebase. Check hydration, persistence, and clearing of CI_FIX_REBASE_PENDING across RunContext, monitor iterations, state-file writes, and retry paths. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
